It's interesting to see the WCST Spoilers 7.0's speculation as to what
will be in the next version, 3.1 as of that time.  Obviously everyone
was expecting bug-fixes, instead of the resulting massive revision of
the game:

----------

"Expected In Version 3.1.
Many people have wondered about the fabled version 3.1 of NetHack.
This new version has been in the works by the NetHack "Dev Team" for a
period of more than a year now, and it is still hush-hush, with no
release date(s) given or projected. We have, however, managed to glean
a few pieces of information about version 3.1 of NetHack, and have
included them here for you.

"Stop drooling!

"All right then... On to the details:

"Messages will be more verbose when you are using artifacts. For
instance, Stormbringer currently tells you "The black blade drains
life from the (insert poor hapless creature's name here)." Fire brand,
for instance, might say "The fiery blade burns the (monster)," or, if
the monster was immune, "The (monster) seems not to be affected by the
flame of your blade." "

---This happened, although it seems like an extremely minor thing now.

"The bug that has been running around for quite some time now which
allows bags of holding to hold basically limitless quantities of stuff
(by playing with the blessed/cursed status of the bag) will be fixed.
Thus, some of the scores that were being obtained by dilithium
crystaldiving will be much more difficult to get, because the amount
of dilithium you can carry out of the dungeon will be severely
limited."

---To think they were still worried about people getting huge scores
from dilithium crystals back in those days of pre MAXINT-1 scoring!

"The entire vision and display system of NetHack has been re-written.
Among other things, this will fix the annoying problem of teleported
stuff not showing up on your screen or creating blank spots randomly
scattered around the screen. Question: will this mean that NetHack
will now have an improved line of sight algorithm, similar to the one
currently being used in Moria?"

---This happened, in fact the wiki notes LOS as one of the more
fundamental changes in 3.1.

"New ranged effects have been added. This will allow, for instance,
fireballs to go until they hit a monster and then explode in a radius
around that monster, instead of just going in a line like they
currently do. It is also rumored that various other cloud type effects
will be included."

---We finally got scrolls of stinking cloud in 3.3, many years after
3.1.

"There will supposedly be several new special levels and/or rooms,
although no details as to what exactly these will be are available.
Also, NetHack's level handling capabilities have been re-written so
that it will now be very easy for the Dev Team (and others!) to add in
new special levels or new special rooms."

Most of the rooms turned out to be one form of lair or another.  Some
more were added a while later.  The level compiler turned out to be
rather fidgety.

"It is rumored that some "NetHack Abuses" have been made impossible.
Specifically, paralyzing the Wizard of Yendor and taking advantage of
kicking sinks have supposedly been fixed or limited. "

Ah, the ancient paralyze-the-wizard bug.  In those days, a popular
tactic was to paralyze the Wizard of Yendor with a potion of
paralysis, then leave the level.  The game knew he was still
paralyzed, but because he was off the level his paralysis counter
wasn't updated, effectively taking him out of the game.  Sinks were
modified so only one ring, succubus and black pudding could be made
from one, although in the case of black puddings this turned out to be
a half-measure at best.

